.swiftpm/xcode/
# Package.resolved is deliberately NOT ignored. The convention is that libraries float and
# applications pin, and this repo ships an application: `swift-transformers` and
# `swift-huggingface` are declared `from:`, and Package.swift records that their versions were
# chosen to satisfy a macro's expanded API surface. Without the lockfile a fresh clone can resolve
# a newer minor release and fail to build for reasons a contributor cannot be expected to diagnose,
# and CI has nothing stable to key its dependency cache on.

# Build artifacts
build/
*.o
*.dylib

# Models & corpora — large binaries, never committed
# (recipe sidecars are small and MAY be committed; model checkpoints and RAW corpora are not)
*.gguf
*.mlx
*.safetensors
/corpus/
/models/
# Weights staged for bundling by scripts/stage-model.sh. 1.6 GB belongs in the release bundle,
# assembled at package time — not in the history of every clone.
/Vendor/

# Editor cruft
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Pre-launch working notes. Deliberately not published: working notes,
# what to do about specific commits, and personal details — internal judgement calls, not decisions.
# The decisions themselves live in docs/DECISIONS.md, and the release *process* is docs/RELEASING.md.
# Working notes kept out of the repository. A pattern rather than a filename: an ignore
# rule naming one file tells every reader that that exact file exists.
*.local.md

# Built application bundles and disk images. 1.7 GB of app does not belong in git — it is
# assembled by scripts/package-app.sh and attached to a GitHub release.
/dist/

# Scratch git worktrees created by tooling that builds a second revision alongside this one
# (comparing two releases, isolating a change). They contain a whole checkout plus its build
# directory, and a stray one turns `git status` into noise at exactly the moment you are trying
# to read a diff.
/.claude/worktrees/
